{title: My Soul Waits in Silence}
{subtitle: Psalms 62:1–2}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 6/8}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Gm7] | [Gm7] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
My soul waits [Bb]in silence for [Gm7]God alone
From [Eb]Him comes my salvation
He is my rock and [Bb]my salvation
My [Eb]stronghold in this world
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I [Bb]will never be [Gm7]badly shaken
My soul waits in silence
[Eb]From Him comes my salvation
My [Bb]soul waits in silence
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
You all assail a [Gm7]man to break him down
Like a lean[Eb]ing wall tottering
Like a fence that cannot stand
[Bb]You plot to bring him down
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I will never be badly shak[Gm7]en
My soul waits in silence
From Him comes [Eb]my salvation
My soul waits [Bb]in silence
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
They take [Eb]pleasure in falsehood
With their mouths [Bb]they bless
Inwardly they [Gm7]curse
My soul rests [Eb]in truth
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
For He alone is my rock
My salvation [Gm7]my stronghold
My soul waits in si[Eb]lence
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |
